<title>USA: Biodynamics bone allografts approved.</title>
<headline>Biodynamics bone allografts approved.</headline>
<dateline>TAMPA, Fla. 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Biodynamics International Inc said on Thursday that its Tutoplast processed bone allografts have received official approval for distribution in France after being kept out of the market since 1995.</p>
<p>The company's Tutoplast, which is used for bone repairs such as hip replacement operations, was prohibited from being used in France due to a change of regulations that were in effect in 1995, Biodynamics said.</p>
<p>All allografts had to go through a new approval process after the rule change, which entailed an evaluation by a microbiology expert committee, Biodynamics said.</p>
<p>Prior to these changes in regulatory requirements, France had been Biodynamics' largest market for Tutoplast processed bone allografts in Europe.</p>
</text>
